{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_5eb3e72825e6d10306645adce4fe2a85f1652ff8629bac52644c047ab29854c1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The intent-lock feature adds core files intent.ts, scope-audit.ts, glob.ts, and stable-json.ts, with the scope audit composed inside verifyCommand rather than as a standalone authoritative command."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9fe03ac6c24a79c2eb41f18ca165e2426c5558925e9a4b520f1ded755b3eb655"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is intended to stay zero-dependency, using only Bun and node: builtins; the boundary forbids adding npm packages for glob matching, signature verification, or JSON canonicalization."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a3013de4a7d0fb3024bd1409eaf0ad792e71886313a4c78780bbaceb97627f58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes subcommands including init, red, green, refactor, verify, revise-test, status, doctor, inspect-test, prompt, and lock-intent, invoked via Bun with flags like --goal-id, --test, --protect, --ci, --replay."}],"claim_ids":["clm_5eb3e72825e6d10306645adce4fe2a85f1652ff8629bac52644c047ab29854c1","clm_9fe03ac6c24a79c2eb41f18ca165e2426c5558925e9a4b520f1ded755b3eb655","clm_a3013de4a7d0fb3024bd1409eaf0ad792e71886313a4c78780bbaceb97627f58"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276","id":"pg_092837e4623350b9af678750316378d6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kingbootoshi-rgr-docs-prds-intent-lock-scope-audit-intent-boundary-md--8750316378d6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f643615a30725a0a9f54396e31684599"],"title":"kingbootoshi/rgr/docs/prds/intent-lock-scope-audit.intent-boundary.md @ 45ffc907a54b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_4702a081ce6d335ccf9e4fd376328f52de026ad8c3153c8871fb4bcd6abdecd1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md instructs contributors to write the failing test first, capture Red via `bun run rgr -- red --strict`, change production code only after Red, then run green, refactor, and `verify --ci --replay` before handoff, and to use `rgr revise-test` rather than editing protected Red tests."}],"claim_ids":["clm_4702a081ce6d335ccf9e4fd376328f52de026ad8c3153c8871fb4bcd6abdecd1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276","id":"pg_29a378f3b6605be4b32b12731ce8231c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kingbootoshi-rgr-agents-md-45ffc907a54b-12731ce8231c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d29acc6cf52f53cb9f627d97309c2884"],"title":"kingbootoshi/rgr/AGENTS.md @ 45ffc907a54b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_7a7e15276d199b5f1029eb452432b92426960ecfc851a2600e50e27f774e2451"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"docs/EVALS.md describes deterministic Tier 1 harness checks (no model judge) that verify the production RGR proof layers reject known bad agent behaviors such as helper tampering, changed Green commands, non-bun-test proofs, and Red self-mutation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_7a7e15276d199b5f1029eb452432b92426960ecfc851a2600e50e27f774e2451"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276","id":"pg_676e681a65e85b32a8dc87c47d722d90","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kingbootoshi-rgr-docs-evals-md-45ffc907a54b-87c47d722d90.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1e870c1098b35abe93e08e49acb43c30"],"title":"kingbootoshi/rgr/docs/EVALS.md @ 45ffc907a54b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276","id":"pg_834a2deb80505ecb8b7bc006318f17fc","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kingbootoshi-rgr-docs-prds-ac-manifest-txt-45ffc907a54b-c006318f17fc.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_96d512861be05522858c5f2b52a39fdf"],"title":"kingbootoshi/rgr/docs/prds/ac-manifest.txt @ 45ffc907a54b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_41f7efe1058853cd503512261dc36bb04e738500a18948ce51c8de77d7bd92c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Enforcement rules include: Red must fail, Red defaults to test-surface changes only, protected Red files are hashed with SHA-256 and snapshotted, Green runs the exact Red command, and strict Red protects imported helpers, fixtures, snapshots, test config, and lockfiles."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4812ceee52e841b721437d7eca50668dc25ec8882b0fff47abc972b1dced1ede"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every command proof uses the argv after the -- separator, and per the enforcement list this is currently direct `bun test` only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_725688658c0766c43e2e7d9aa797385dcd83c7b2c82a014ca5966ae1277699a5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every rgr run writes .rgr/manifest.json, .rgr/events.jsonl, snapshots, diffs, and command output logs as an audit trail."},{"claim_ids":["clm_83cc8a355c6e7f664c9654fb2eefe1423a1bb18b787130102f44b202daf01e85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The threat model states that an agent with unrestricted write access to the same repo can still delete .rgr or bypass the CLI, so local use is a discipline gate and authoritative results require running verify inside CI, sandboxes, or agent harnesses."},{"claim_ids":["clm_97b577b99e2bb8835a5a8995c6b359c688078e46abc77cc1812284ddc3da761e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"rgr is described as a no-dependency Red-Green-Refactor gate for coding agents that records the failing test first, freezes it with hashes and snapshots, and refuses Green or Refactor if the Red test was edited."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9ef1c58777b257877c2dc78e4c15b46fdc9430f6dfe0373fd4e4456f4fdc7cd5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"RGR ships two skills as Claude Code and Codex plugins: the rgr skill and intent-contract, which compiles a signed Locked Intent Boundary into an IntentLock that `rgr verify --intent-lock` enforces."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a3013de4a7d0fb3024bd1409eaf0ad792e71886313a4c78780bbaceb97627f58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes subcommands including init, red, green, refactor, verify, revise-test, status, doctor, inspect-test, prompt, and lock-intent, invoked via Bun with flags like --goal-id, --test, --protect, --ci, --replay."}],"claim_ids":["clm_41f7efe1058853cd503512261dc36bb04e738500a18948ce51c8de77d7bd92c7","clm_4812ceee52e841b721437d7eca50668dc25ec8882b0fff47abc972b1dced1ede","clm_725688658c0766c43e2e7d9aa797385dcd83c7b2c82a014ca5966ae1277699a5","clm_83cc8a355c6e7f664c9654fb2eefe1423a1bb18b787130102f44b202daf01e85","clm_97b577b99e2bb8835a5a8995c6b359c688078e46abc77cc1812284ddc3da761e","clm_9ef1c58777b257877c2dc78e4c15b46fdc9430f6dfe0373fd4e4456f4fdc7cd5","clm_a3013de4a7d0fb3024bd1409eaf0ad792e71886313a4c78780bbaceb97627f58"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276","id":"pg_8ccb89e973f05cc9b1f7bebd91636482","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kingbootoshi-rgr-readme-md-45ffc907a54b-bebd91636482.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d50b118cb4605c69b519bdd47bd0cf4b"],"title":"kingbootoshi/rgr/README.md @ 45ffc907a54b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:03:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_69acd873cd044343bac3bedd47967276"}
